  "body": "Last week a few community members, including the active HTML spec editors @annevk and @domenic, had a video call to triage some of the open issues. We spent an hour in a focused, high-bandwidth discussion and made some progress on a few spec issues. Here are the action items from that meeting:\r\n\r\n1. @past to file an issue for the next meeting, inviting broader participation and announcing the agenda.\r\n2. @annevk (or others) to create an [Agenda] tag for adding issues to the agenda.\r\n3. On #5959, @mfreed7 and @annevk to take a look after the meeting and comment on PR.\r\n4. @mfreed7 and @annevk to analyze #6287, ideally with someone from WebKit as well. [This comment](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6287#issuecomment-762754827) summarizes the proposed spec vs. current browser behavior story.\r\n5. @mfreed7 to review #6283.\r\n6. @mfreed7 and @annevk to look into [this SVG issue](https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/issues/179).\r\n\r\nThis exercise seemed worthwhile so we will be repeating it on March 4th, 9 am PST for an hour. If you are interested in attending the next call please respond here or reach out privately to me or the spec editors. We will be tagging issues for the next call using the [agenda+ label](https://github.com/whatwg/html/labels/agenda%2B) and we would like to invite anyone that can contribute to said issues to join us. ",
